anting to take this job  because they have to throw their life on  the line uh but we'll see how it plays  out and jeanette what's next for  nicholas cruz's case  well his trial date has not been  scheduled yet and his lawyers have said  that he would plead guilty in exchange  for the death penalty being taken off  the table prosecutors have not agreed to  do that they want this case to go to a  jury and cruz is scheduled to be back in  court next week for hearings on several  motions all right so those are two  potential trials coming out of this this  school shooting we'll see how it plays  out of course give you updates as it  continues coming up on law on crime  daily durst's sixth day on  cross-examination his clap back to the  prosecutor plus an iconic album cover  and why the subject is suing the band 30  years later exclusive legal analysis  after the break  [Music]  we're back and it's not smelling much  like teen spirit for the famous nirvana  album never mind the man who was the  infant photographed on the cover is now  suing claiming the image is child  pornography  spencer eldon was four months old when  he was photographed for one of the most  iconic album covers of all time  nirvana's 1991 album never mind it was  widely interpreted that the album cover  depicting a naked baby in a pool  reaching out for a dollar bill on a fish  hook is an anti-capitalism statement  eldon however now has a different  interpretation the now 30 year old is  suing the remaining members of the ban  kirk cobain's estate and the record  company on grounds of child pornography  stating that his infant self portrays a  sex worker the lawsuit states that  defendants intentionally commercially  marketed spencer's child pornography and  leveraged the shocking nature of his  image to promote themselves and their  music at his expense  the now adult is known for recreating  the album cover with swim trunks on on  multiple occasions most recently on the  25th anniversary of the album's release  for the record we're not showing the  full picture there of the album cover  just so you know but let's bring back  legal analyst dina dahl and co-host  terry austin to make sense of his iconic  album cover terry is this a case about  child pornography that nirvana profited  from this cover and he did not or  something different altogether  brian this is one of the most bizarre  cases i have ever seen first of all  eldon took advantage of this cover photo  and it gave him fame and now all of a  sudden he's claiming that it's child  pornography and technically under the  definition you have to have some sort of  involvement or sexually explicit  something on the picture and that  doesn't exist here and i think the fact  that he has been using this should be  used against him and i think the case  should be dismissed altogether i think  to your point he's upset he hasn't  gotten paid and perhaps you know maybe  they should make some payment to him and  the fact that he's been using it all  this time means he's kind of giving  consent yeah i wouldn't be surprised if  we hear about a settlement on the side  in this case goes away  uh dina in the original cover you can  definitely see it all but does this fit  the definition of child pornography or  is it perhaps artwork  right and that's the thing one of the  exceptions to child pornography is that  there is a serious artistic merit and  you can hear this was on a music cover  that's actually been on it for such a  long time that if the public had had  some sort of reaction right usually  pornography kind of is based on how  people react to it we would have had an  outcry when this first came out so you  could argue very easily that this is  similar to  naked pictures of children that we see  in art museums all the time  it could also have some sort of a  contractual argument it's unclear  whether or not his parents clearly  consented to the nudity of this picture  and what he's asking for only 150  dollars per defendant seems so  reasonable that i imagine we're going to  have a settlement in this case and it  won't actually go to trial absolutely it  would be interesting to see the trial  but i agree with you dina that a  settlement is probably the closest thing  that we're going to see on the horizon  for this case thank you both when we  come back robert durst thinks kathy  might still be alive how the prosecutor  is fighting what he thinks are lies from  the accused murderer  [Music]  welcome back we're back in california  for the 50th day of robert durst's  murder trial and day six of robert durst  cross-examination  robert durst is testifying in his own  defense claiming that he did not murder  his best friend susan berman execution  style in december 2000 it is alleged  that susan had exclusive information  about robert durst's missing wife kathy  a murder that the real estate heir is  also accused of investigators say berman  placed a phone call pretending to be  durst's missing wife to call in sick to  her medical school rotation outside the  presence of the jury the judge gave his  opinion on the matter  i think there's overwhelming evidence  that susan berman  made made the call  and that  there's overwhelming evidence that susan  berman did make the call the question  here is  is the implication is that no one else  would have done it there is no one else  and so the the the what the people are  that people are entitled to present  their theory if there's any evidence to  support it  then when the juror was brought in  things got heated on the stand with  lewin and duras trying to get under each  other's skin this was met with  interesting remarks from the defendant  are you stalling for time right now is  that what this is about i'm just  scrolling for time i'm in jail overruled  he asked the witness if he's stalling  for time the witnesses let's assume  you're lying right now  let's assume i'm telling the truth right  now well that can be that can be a 